cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "DeScideratum: Citation-as-Invocation in Scientific Publishing"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Karmarkar"
    given-names: "Prasanna Varun"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-2284-6914"
repository-code: "https://github.com/prakar/DeScideratum"
url: "https://prakar.github.io/DeScideratum/"
abstract: >
  A research prototype investigating citation-as-invocation in scientific
  publishing: whether a scientific citation can be a live, runnable function
  call rather than a static reference. Includes three verified citation
  lineages (resampling, multiple-testing, meta-analysis) and cite-invoke, a
  MyST Markdown directive unifying citation and execution into a single
  authoring construct.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - scientific-publishing
  - mystmd
  - citation
  - open-science
  - pyodide
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-07-30"
